      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David J. Nathanson",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The trial judge found Melvin Smith not guilty on the merits and unequivocally so. That acquittal entitled Melvin Smith to repose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cathryn A. Neaves",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State, on the other hand, asks this Court to make exceptions to the rule, long-held, that acquittals terminate jeopardy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David J. Nathanson",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Double Jeopardy Clause is a constitutional policy of finality for the defendant's benefit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So would you explain to me if there's any practical effect to your winning in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the reason you didn't want a fairly simple rule that I was thinking of? I'll tell you what it is and you'll tell me honestly why you don't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Neaves",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position has been consistent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in fact, the -- the quick and dirty procedure you describe is probably a boon to prosecutors because a judge is -- is not likely to take the serious step of dismissing a charge on the basis of -- of such a procedure and is more likely to say, well, we'll let the trial go ahead and see what the evidence discloses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Srinivasan",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The trial court in this case was permitted to correct its erroneous ruling in favor of the defendant on the motion for judgment of acquittal. Because the prosecution is entitled to a full and fair opportunity to prove its case, that's a value --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The trial court in this case was permitted to correct its erroneous ruling in favor of the defendant on the motion for judgment of acquittal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Honing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nathanson",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Souter, I want to heartily endorse the -- the way you phrased what the rule should be, which is, trial judges, you ought to take this seriously."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-8661",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4e7a706e18bfcda1adabe91421dd3e1f23627b3a9f6bf63a9b795b0354088ea5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4e7a706e18bf-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
